  "$schema": "fbench/v1",
  "name": "Esso Libya 18 m equivalent LNG trench fire (1969)",
  "citation": "May, W.G. and McQueen, W. (1973), Esso tests in Libya, reported in: Raj, P.K. (2005). Large LNG Fire Thermal Radiation - Modeling Issues & Hazard Criteria Revisited. Process Safety Progress 24(3), 192-202. Table 1, 'Summary of LNG Fire Experiments'.",
  "dataConfidence": "Medium",
  "description": "Continuous LNG feed into a 70 m x 25 m land dike (trench), 18 m equivalent diameter. Table 1 of Raj (2005): regression 1.6e-4 m/s, wide-angle mean emissive power 92 kW/m2, radiated fraction 12-16%. The lowest emissive power in the LNG series and a useful outlier: the geometry is a long trench, not a circular pool, so a cylindrical solid-flame model is being pushed outside its shape assumption.",
